{"name":"Gameboy Screen","hex":"#8bac0f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"screen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A physical barrier that shelters or hides.\nA physical divider intended to block an area from view, or provide shelter from something dangerous.","A physical divider intended to block an area from view, or provide shelter from something dangerous."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To filter by passing through a screen.","To filter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Game Boy","blocks":[{"text":"The Game Boy is a handheld game console developed and marketed by Nintendo. It was released in Japan on April 21, 1989, followed by North America on July 31, 1989 and Europe on September 28, 1990. Nintendo's first handheld to use ROM cartridges, it succeeded the Game & Watch line of handheld electronic games and competed with Sega's Game Gear, Atari's Lynx, and NEC's TurboExpress in the fourth generation of video game consoles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Game-Boy-FL.png/330px-Game-Boy-FL.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy","wikidata":"Q186437"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Game_Boy_originale.jpg/500px-Game_Boy_originale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Game_Boy_originale.jpg/1280px-Game_Boy_originale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Game_Boy_originale.jpg/500px-Game_Boy_originale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Original gray Game Boy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGame_Boy_originale.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/